{"title":"Sequence","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p>A <b>sequence</b> is an ordered list of terms.  Sequences may be either <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Finite\" title=\"Finite\">finite</a> or <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Infinite\" title=\"Infinite\">infinite</a>.\n</p>\n<div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Definition\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Definition</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Convergence\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Convergence</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Monotone_Sequences\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Monotone Sequences</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Resources\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Resources</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Definition\">Definition</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Sequence&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Definition\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A sequence of real numbers is simply a function <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/9/e59b3c742da1f04d4585693e2c77c6bc0425bf6b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f : \\mathbb{N} \\rightarrow \\mathbb{R}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"79\" height=\"16\" />. For instance, the function <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/d/0dda5d9cc1f37a095f591d50370589b47e20111c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x) = x^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"76\" height=\"19\" /> defined on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/e/a1e6cd0e4103015efba12e0fc4291f012b467eaa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathbb{N}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> corresponds to the sequence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/6/4b62d94fd526d04e473659ed60bc362b4a623c54.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X = (x_n) = (0, 1, 4, 9, 16, \\ldots)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"227\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Convergence\">Convergence</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Sequence&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Convergence\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Intuitively, a sequence <b>converges</b> if its terms approach a particular number.\n</p><p>Formally, a sequence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/b/6dbd595b1babd5be7ff1c5a33907b992f2e847b5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x_n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"32\" height=\"18\" /> of reals converges to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/4/d/44d50fdf8c7c6ac3f17261ffbd5a6f7edda262f4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$L \\in \\mathbb{R}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"47\" height=\"13\" /> if and only if for all positive reals <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/a/f/eaf4418fbe935c15a606516d8f55dc380cd8e822.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\epsilon$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"7\" height=\"8\" />, there exists a positive integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> such that for all integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/6/bd614aab3401d541b41d996669ed8ab088c7fc77.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\ge k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"44\" height=\"15\" />, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/6/af6cf377f917d474d417df1bd2d1e06964498e4b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|x_n - L| &lt; \\epsilon$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"98\" height=\"20\" />.  If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/b/6dbd595b1babd5be7ff1c5a33907b992f2e847b5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x_n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"32\" height=\"18\" /> converges to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/9/859ccf4cd60c7bc6b8fa1afc9a42dc811a826d6f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$L$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/9/859ccf4cd60c7bc6b8fa1afc9a42dc811a826d6f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$L$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> is called the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Limit\" title=\"Limit\">limit</a> of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/b/6dbd595b1babd5be7ff1c5a33907b992f2e847b5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x_n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"32\" height=\"18\" /> and is written <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/2/54258610d65a68355ed7200839abd550c1a130a3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\lim_{n \\to \\infty} x_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"56\" height=\"23\" />. The statement that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/b/6dbd595b1babd5be7ff1c5a33907b992f2e847b5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x_n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"32\" height=\"18\" /> converges to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/9/859ccf4cd60c7bc6b8fa1afc9a42dc811a826d6f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$L$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> can be written as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/9/5/995260a5d3ffd3e2a836bf10e40c972de2cc6dbd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x_n)\\rightarrow L$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"74\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>A classic example of convergence would be to show that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26e26e9a4fd5e603d239f93cbe802caf76b1feff.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1/n\\to 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"68\" height=\"20\" /> as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/4/694a761d1744afe15db60a60ee38458b687488d4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n\\to \\infty$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"56\" height=\"10\" />.  \n</p><p><b>Claim</b>: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/6/e/d6e96cde4eba8c1b24679596b5f9b7d6d91b398d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\lim_{n\\to\\infty}\\frac{1}{n}=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"85\" height=\"37\" />.  \n</p><p><i>Proof</i>: Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/4/ca47de052eb3fb5454694d9bce3561ebff831a1e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\epsilon&gt;0$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"40\" height=\"13\" /> be arbitrary and choose <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/c/33c4612b1b4030bdf3637868f804bfdc45d663b1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N&gt;\\frac{1}{\\epsilon}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"56\" height=\"38\" />.  Then for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/5/845c0da210ec3bb12d45628b74e37402799d9695.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n\\ge N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"54\" height=\"17\" /> we see that\n</p>\n<center><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/b/b/cbb6bfc590019eae8754fd9dc52f97f32a42772a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n&gt;\\frac{1}{\\epsilon}\\implies \\frac{1}{n}&lt;\\epsilon\\implies \\left|\\frac{1}{n}-0\\right|&lt;\\epsilon$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"285\" height=\"45\" /></center>  \n<p>which proves that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/1/1911c83345cd1fd5a0af45535c561ade7891cbff.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|x_n-L|&lt;\\epsilon$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"98\" height=\"20\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26e26e9a4fd5e603d239f93cbe802caf76b1feff.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1/n\\to 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"68\" height=\"20\" /> as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/4/694a761d1744afe15db60a60ee38458b687488d4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n\\to \\infty$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"56\" height=\"10\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/c/b6cf65b1f2fbdf388e3daeff9b96b34d3399d777.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\square$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Monotone_Sequences\">Monotone Sequences</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Sequence&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Monotone Sequences\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Many significant sequences have their terms continually increasing, such as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/a/b/3ab86e31a4c2c9f0a6307731f5e1d32618e88d5d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(n^2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"31\" height=\"19\" />, or continually decreasing, such as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c522206264dfd9f2ebacdc6a81cfaea288c2328.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1/n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"41\" height=\"18\" />. This motivates the following definitions:\n</p><p>A sequence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/0/f/c0f65c4493b9dfbdb707da570faff76015a7f44d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(p_n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"31\" height=\"18\" /> of reals is said to be\n</p>\n<ul><li><b>increasing</b> if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/c/43ce7907290b207011a30923aa453920b884bb8a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p_n\\leq p_{n+1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"76\" height=\"16\" /> for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/4/a64508262bb2272e129bd59c31142b17e78b6ad3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n\\in\\mathbb{N}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"48\" height=\"15\" /> and <b>strictly increasing</b> if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/8/548662efd6506db9c1f23d0e3fe9fd4439fde54a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p_n&lt;p_{n+1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"76\" height=\"14\" /> for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/4/a64508262bb2272e129bd59c31142b17e78b6ad3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n\\in\\mathbb{N}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"48\" height=\"15\" />,</li>\n<li><b>decreasing</b> if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/a/9/ea9cc7a3b6d622f9d5d93f967064fba786806c48.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p_n\\geq p_{n+1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"76\" height=\"16\" /> for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/4/a64508262bb2272e129bd59c31142b17e78b6ad3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n\\in\\mathbb{N}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"48\" height=\"15\" /> and <b>strictly decreasing</b> if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/c/a4ca2cb15f0b4386451f5779034d292f61986b5e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p_n&gt;p_{n+1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"79\" height=\"16\" /> for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/4/a64508262bb2272e129bd59c31142b17e78b6ad3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n\\in\\mathbb{N}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"48\" height=\"15\" />,</li>\n<li><b>monotone</b> if it is either decreasing or increasing.</li></ul>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Resources\">Resources</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Sequence&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Resources\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.research.att.com/~njas/sequences/\">Online Encyclopedia of Integer Sequences</a></li></ul>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Sequence&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Arithmetic_sequence\" title=\"Arithmetic sequence\">Arithmetic sequence</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Geometric_sequence\" title=\"Geometric sequence\">Geometric sequence</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Bolzano-Weierstrass_Theorem\" title=\"Bolzano-Weierstrass Theorem\">Bolzano-Weierstrass Theorem</a></li></ul>\n<p><i>This article is a stub.  Help us out by <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=Sequence&amp;action=edit\">expanding it</a></span>.</i>\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018110228\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.024 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.039 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 224/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 265/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 4/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 7379/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    5.920      1 Template:Stub\n100.00%    5.920      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:2018:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018110228 and revision id 181350. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}